How about this approach to include three ways of transfer flows:
1. Transfer X amount from this pot to other pot
2. Receive X amount from other pot to this pot
3. Adjust final amount to this pot
But we will limit to single pot to single pot only.

-- User clicks on Transfer button on pot card

<Screen 1>
Reallocate Funds
<Pot Name> <Current Amount>
-----
Replace Transfer text to a drop down with three display options (Send, Receive, Adjust To) Default will be "Send"

Dynamic placement of the Right side Pots dropdown and field title text:
- When "send" is selected(Mostly the existing flow):
    - Pots dropdown title text: "To Pot"
- When "receive" is selected:
    - Pots dropdown title text: "From Pot"
    - Reverse the arrow direction.
- When "adjust to" is selected:
    - If the resulting operation requires sending the amount to other pot(Functionally same as "Send" but with a note below the amount field):
            - Below amount field, show a text: "Send <x> amount to other pot"
            - Pots dropdown title text: "To Pot"
            - Point the arrow to the right.
    - If the resulting operation requires receiving the amount from other pot (Functionally same as "Receive" but with a note below the amount field)::
        - Below amount field, show a text: "Receive <x> amount from other pot"
        - Pots dropdown title text: "From Pot"
        - Point the arrow to the left.








